From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:44:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] assurance.watch: the component that runs when nobody is
 looking
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WHY
  Every other domain here is invoked by somebody who already suspects
  something. Nothing in this package does anything between invocations, which
  means nothing in it justifies a monthly price. A watch finds a change on the
  day it happened rather than the day somebody remembered to look, and that is
  the difference between a tool licence and a subscription.

WHAT
  src/assurance/watch/config.py  the standing instruction: these machines,
                                  these plans, these folders, this cadence
  src/assurance/watch/runner.py  one pass — collect, compare, seal only what
                                  moved, report only what is new
  src/assurance/watch/cli.py     run / status, with exit codes as the interface
  deploy/assurance/WATCH.md      the four judgements and a real three weeks

CUSTOMER VALUE
  Week 2's export headers moved on every machine — new timestamp, new
  operator, new sequence number, four items each — and the run reads QUIET.
  Week 3 one protective zone was reshaped and the run names the item, the
  safety function and the machine. A report that is silent when nothing
  happened is the only kind anybody still reads in month six.

RISK
  Four decisions, because this is the surface where a wrong default turns into
  a report nobody opens:

  Seal only on change, but record every look. Forty identical manifests a week
  would drown the real ones; a ledger with no record at all cannot tell "we
  looked and it was the same" from "we never looked", and those are opposite
  facts. Every run seals a lightweight observation; a manifest only when the
  configuration actually moved.

  New is not outstanding. A finding already reported is demoted, not repeated,
  and does not make the run a finding.

  Uncollectable is not unchanged. A missing export folder is an absence of
  observation, not an observation of absence, and it exits 2, never 0.

  Silence expires. A watch that stopped running looks exactly like a fleet that
  stopped changing. max_age_hours turns that ambiguity into an alarm.

  A run also never ends before it began: when the clock is injected the whole
  run reads from it.

ROLLBACK
  git revert this commit. Outside assurance/watch it touches one CLI domain
  and one ruff ignore.

TESTS
  596 passed (36 new), ruff clean. Asserted: a week where only the export
  headers moved is quiet and seals no manifest but still records the look; a
  real change is reported the week it happens with its item and its safety
  function; a repeated finding is demoted; a removed export folder degrades the
  run; and a machine nobody could collect goes stale rather than silent.

SUCCESS CONDITION
  One customer's Monday morning email is empty for three weeks running, and on
  the fourth it names a serial number they had not been told about.

